AFFIDAVIT

I, Dr. Anil Kumar Verma, S/o Late Shri Rameshwar Verma, aged 52 years,
residing at 5, Ratanada, Jodhpur – 342 001,
Highway Engineering Consultant,
do hereby solemnly affirm and state as follows:

1. I am a qualified Highway Engineer with 28 years of experience in NHAI projects
   and have been engaged as a consultant by M/s. Roadcon Infra Pvt. Ltd. for the
   NH-148B Extension Project.

2. I have personally inspected the construction site on multiple occasions and have
   reviewed all technical drawings, variation orders, and quality compliance records.

3. Regarding the revised alignment (VO-001): The alignment shift of 200-500 meters
   in certain sections was indeed necessary to avoid ecological zones and protected
   forest areas. This was a valid engineering decision by NHAI.

4. The additional 3.2 km work due to revised alignment should be compensated as per
   NHAI GCC Clause 12 (Variations). The rate analysis prepared by my office shows
   that the fair compensation for this additional work is ₹4.92 Crore.

5. Regarding quality of work: I have personally inspected all earthwork, sub-grade,
   bituminous surfacing, and bridge construction. The quality is fully compliant with:
   - IRC 37:2018 (Guidelines for Design of Flexible Pavements)
   - IRC 78:2014 (Standard Specifications and Code of Practice for Road Bridges)
   - MoRTH (Ministry of Road Transport & Highways) Specifications

6. Test certificates for all bituminous mixes (Marshall Stability tests) show 100%
   compliance with target stability values. No structural deficiencies have been identified.

7. Regarding the suspension of work: The contractor's suspension on 15.04.2022 was
   valid under FIDIC Clause 16 (Suspension for Non-Payment) as NHAI had not paid
   3 certified running bills aggregating ₹2.14 Crore for over 60 days.

8. Regarding utility shifting: It is a well-established principle in highway construction
   that utility shifting is the Employer's responsibility. The 210-day delay due to
   electric poles not being shifted is a clear case of Employer's delay.

9. Regarding forest clearance: Forest clearance is a statutory requirement and the
   timeline for clearance is beyond the contractor's control. The 240-day delay in
   forest clearance is a valid ground for Extension of Time.

10. All facts stated above are within my professional knowledge and are true to the best of my
    information and belief. No part of it is false and nothing material has been concealed.

Deponent: Dr. Anil Kumar Verma
Date: 01.12.2022
Place: Jodhpur

Sworn before me:
Oath Commissioner / Notary Public